      "writtenOn": "2023-06-12T18:33:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I double checked everything and -Wno-format is the right choice. I retract my suggestion. \n\nThe build is linux 64-bit and it is specifying `%ld` for a `ptrdiff_t`. \nThis is _technically_ wrong--`%ld` is for `long`s, not `ptrdiff_t`s. It should really be `%td`. It\u0027s harmless in practice, since a `ptrdiff_t` in Linux 64-bit is the same size and signedness as a `long`. \n\nPerhaps this code is intended to work on pre-C++11 standard libraries.\n\nWe might want a comment here (`# EXPAT_FMT_PTRDIFF_T uses outdated format specifiers`) but it\u0027s NBD.",
      "parentUuid": "2af9778c_f28917ab",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 53,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 53,
        "endChar": 28
      },
