      },
      "lineNbr": 76,
      "author": {
        "id": 20044
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-06-12T18:39:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You\u0027re right I was able to simplify it after all. I *did* run into issues with the \"\\0\" character which is why I switched to a char vector, but actually it\u0027s only when it\u0027s in a string literal (e.g. const std::string sig \u003d \"http://ns.adobe.com/xmp/extension/\\0\"; won\u0027t include the \u0027\\0\u0027) and I extrapolated a bit too much from that. As soon as you have a std::string then it\u0027s fine.\nThey introduced std::literals::string_literals in c++14 to fix this.",
      "parentUuid": "01974776_a826b3af",
